  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Stablecoin market cap fell 3.1% over 30D:</strong> Stablecoin market cap at $285.89B (3.1% lower over 30D). Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/tech/2026/11/02/xrp-ledger-set-to-fix-flaw-that-could-let-stablecoin-partners-print-new-tokens\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">XRP Ledger set to fix flaw that could have let stablecoin partners print new tokens</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Stablecoin market structure remains concentration-led:</strong> leadership is still defined by a small set of large issuers/platforms; share shifts matter as much as aggregate market-cap growth. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/hong-kong-24-7-tokenized-settlements-stablecoin-trials?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hong Kong takes tokenized settlement to 24/7, plans stablecoin trials</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li><li><strong>Policy and reserves are resetting issuer priorities:</strong> Issuer and platform share can shift before aggregate market cap does, because policy and reserve quality determine which names institutions will hold. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/business/2026-11-02-binance-zero-knowledge-proof-of-reserves-snapshot-hack-recovery-432321\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Binance completes latest proof of reserves as it works to restore assets, withdrawals after record hack</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
